From 37ca03578600ff13b33b102015fcb38e1aee8ad6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 14:50:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03286/11362] [outer-loop] adversarial_verify: stop
 quarantining declared control-vs-treatment HONEST NULLS

The TAUTOLOGY check was spuriously flagging the .421 HEADLINE generic_transfer null (exp4556, 4
flags) and the integration-gate null (exp4560) on honest 0.04==0.04 / 2.0074==2.0074 control-vs-
treatment equalities -- the EXPECTED outcome of a no-value ablation, not a two-distinct-metric
fabrication. This FLAGGED/quarantine recurred ~8x across .420/.421, excluding the project's two most
important ARC measurements from capstone aggregation (research_conductor.py:2383-2389).

check_tautology now skips a pair when BOTH: (a) the artifact's own honest_verdict declares a no-value
null (honest_null / no_value_added / no_lever_raises / ...), AND (b) at least one key carries a
control/treatment qualifier (_baseline / _with_verifier / _integrated / _random_router / ...). A
fabrication never self-labels a null, and a generic two-metric coincidence lacks the qualifier -- both
gates are required, so the carve-out cannot whitelist a fabrication. Mirrors the existing
_is_identifier_field and same-family carve-outs.

Verified: exp4556 0 critical (was 4), exp4560 0 critical TAUTOLOGY (was 4; a separate DURATION flag
from its AMBIGUOUS conditional substrate declaration remains -- a conductor-artifact issue, not this
churn). Negatives still flag: celebratory distinct-metric coincidence + honest-null-without-qualifier
both STILL critical. 5 pinned tests + 31 existing adversarial guards green.

This accelerates the LOOP (un-quarantines the headline null so it re-enters aggregation + stops
inflating FLAGGED counts), NOT the metric -- generic_transfer above 0.04 is capability-bound.

